r</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of liver function for hepatic resection</article-title><source>Transplant Proc</source><year>2006</year><volume>38</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>798</fpage><lpage>800</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.transproceed.2006.01.048</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Fazakas J, Mandli T, Ther G, et al. (2006) Evaluation of liver function for hepatic resection. Transplant Proc 38(3):798&#x02013;800 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16647474</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Satoh</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishiyama</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title><sup>99m</sup>Tc-GSA liver dynamic SPECT for the preoperative assessment of hepatectomy</article-title><source>Ann Nucl Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>17</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>67</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Satoh K, Yamamoto Y, Nishiyama Y, et al. (2003) 99mTc-GSA liver dynamic SPECT for the preoperative assessment of hepatectomy. Ann Nucl Med 17(1):61&#x02013;67 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12691132</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR21"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bennink</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dinant</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Erdogan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Preoperative assessment of postoperative remnant liver function using hepatobiliary scintigraphy</article-title><source>J Nucl Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>45</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>965</fpage><lpage>971</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bennink RJ, Dinant S, Erdogan D, et al. (2004) Preoperative assessment of postoperative remnant liver function using hepatobiliary scintigraphy. J Nucl Med 45(6):965&#x02013;971 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15181131</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR22"><label>22.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schindl</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Millar</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Redhead</surname><given-names>DN</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The adaptive response of the reticuloendothelial system to major liver resection in humans</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>2006</year><volume>243</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>507</fpage><lpage>514</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.sla.0000205826.62911.a7</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Schindl MJ, Millar AM, Redhead DN, et al. (2006) The adaptive response of the reticuloendothelial system to major liver resection in humans. Ann Surg 243(4):507&#x02013;514 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16552202</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR23"><label>23.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dejong</surname><given-names>CHC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dowidar</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Wigmore</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Virtual hepatectomy and in vivo urea synthesis in patients with colorectal liver metastases</article-title><source>HPB</source><year>2001</year><volume>3</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>114</fpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Dejong CHC, Dowidar N, Wigmore SJ, et al. (2001)) Virtual hepatectomy and in vivo urea synthesis in patients with colorectal liver metastases. HPB 3(1):114 (abstract) </citation></ref><ref id="CR24"><label>24.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Majeed</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resource and manpower calculations for the provision of hepatobiliary surgical services in the UK</article-title><source>Ann R Coll Surg Engl</source><year>2004</year><volume>86</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1308/003588404322827455</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Majeed AW, Price C (2004) Resource and manpower calculations for the provision of hepatobiliary surgical services in the UK. Ann R Coll Surg Engl 86(2):91&#x02013;95 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15005925</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR25"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Adam</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Laurent</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Azoulay</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Two-stage hepatectomy: a planned strategy to treat irresectable liver tumors</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>232</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>777</fpage><lpage>785</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000658-200012000-00006</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Adam R, Laurent A, Azoulay D, et al. (2000) Two-stage hepatectomy: a planned strategy to treat irresectable liver tumors. Ann Surg 232(6):777&#x02013;785 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11088072</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>Authorship statement; Simon A. W. G. Dello and Ronald M. van Dam contributed equally to the realization of the study and the manuscript and share first authorship.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>